<title>DENMARK: Carlsberg dives on UK Bass ruling.</title>
<headline>Carlsberg dives on UK Bass ruling.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish brewer Carlsberg's shares plunged on Friday after the British government ruled that Bass could not take over joint venture Carlsberg-Tetley and must sell the 50 percent it now owns.</p>
<p>At 1055 GMT, shortly after shares resumed trading, it had fallen 19.1 crowns -- 5.2 percent -- from Thursday's closing 365.1, the level at which it was suspended before the British announcement.</p>
<p>Carlsberg said it was preparing a statement but could not say when it would be ready. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
